# The book's lost update (book/examples/ch13/explore.cb, "Finding the timing
# bugs"): `cobc --explore` must reach both outcomes. The program is decided,
# and its lock is `cb_lock_pathless`, which before the session findings of
# 2026-11-06 passed no turn: a release's pending switch was taken only at a
# later entry into the runtime, and a decided program makes none between its
# unlock and its next lock, so every schedule ran the two bumps one after the
# other (total 2, never 1). (The report is on standard output.)
copy book/examples/ch13/explore.cb explore.cb
run $COBC --cc $CC --explore 40 explore.cb
stdout-has 2 distinct outcomes
stdout-has total 1
stdout-has total 2
